## E3-SPC-v1 Symmetry-Plane Cantilever: half of the 2 x 1 x 1 cantilever, z in [0, 0.5].
## Design domain x in [0, 2.0], y in [0, 1.0], z in [0, 0.5]; cut (symmetry) plane z = 0.5.
## Structured HEX8 mesh, uniform element size 1/24 (48 x 24 x 12 = 13,824 elements, 15,925 nodes).
## Fixed support: all nodes on the x = 0 face (ns_fix). Transverse line load: nodes on the edge
## x = 2, y = 0 spanning z in [0, 0.5] (ns_load). Symmetry sideset: element faces on z = 0.5 (ss_sym).
## Adapted from the candidate Example 7 journal (full 2 x 1 x 1 domain, 48 x 24 x 24, no symmetry plane).
reset
#{len = 2.0}
#{ht  = 1.0}
#{wd  = 0.5}
#{esize = 0.0416667}
## --- geometry: half-width brick with its back-bottom-left corner at the origin ---
create brick x {len} y {ht} z {wd}
move volume 1 x {len/2.0} y {ht/2.0} z {wd/2.0}
## --- structured hex mesh (48 x 24 x 12) ---
volume 1 scheme map
volume 1 size {esize}
mesh volume 1
block 1 volume 1
block 1 name 'block_1'
block 1 element type HEX8
## --- fixed support: the x = 0 face (all displacements) ---
nodeset 1 add node in surface with x_coord < {esize/2.0}
nodeset 1 name "ns_fix"
## --- transverse line load: bottom-right edge (x = len, y = 0), spanning z in [0, wd] ---
nodeset 2 add node with x_coord > {len - esize/2.0} and with y_coord < {esize/2.0}
nodeset 2 name "ns_load"
## --- symmetry (cut) plane: the z = wd face as a sideset ---
sideset 1 add surface with z_coord > {wd - esize/2.0}
sideset 1 name "ss_sym"
export mesh "mesh.exo" dimension 3 overwrite
